A normal chest radiograph shows clear lung fields with fine vascular markings, sharp costophrenic angles, a midline trachea, and a cardiac silhouette of expected size and contour; minor variation may include slightly prominent vascular markings.
Chest radiograph shows symmetric, well-expanded lungs with uniform radiolucency and fine vascular markings, a heart silhouette of expected size and contour, midline mediastinum, sharp costophrenic angles; bronchovascular markings may vary.
Chest X-ray shows clear lung fields with fine vascular markings, sharp costophrenic angles, midline trachea, normal heart size and contours, intact ribs and spine; common variations include inspiratory depth, mild diaphragmatic elevation.
A normal chest X‑ray shows clear, well aerated bilateral lung fields with visible pulmonary vascular markings, a midline trachea, sharp costophrenic angles, and common variations such as mild linear scarring or slight hyperinflation.
A normal chest X-ray shows clear, well-aerated lungs with fine pulmonary vascular markings, sharp costophrenic angles and crisp diaphragm domes, a normal-sized cardiac silhouette, midline trachea and mediastinum.
A normal chest X‑ray shows clear bilateral lung fields with fine, symmetric vascular and bronchovascular markings, sharp costophrenic angles, a centrally positioned mediastinal silhouette with normal cardiac size.
A normal chest X‑ray shows clear lung fields with fine lung markings, a sharp cardiac silhouette, midline trachea, smooth diaphragms with costophrenic angles visible, and expected variations in heart size, and inspiratory depth.
A normal chest X-ray shows clear, well-expanded lungs with visible fine pulmonary markings, sharp cardiomediastinal contours, smooth diaphragm domes; common variations include mild bronchovascular prominence.
A normal chest X-ray shows clear lung fields with visible pulmonary vasculature, sharp costophrenic angles, a central mediastinal silhouette with normal cardiac size, rotation, body habitus, or projection differences.
On a normal chest X‑ray the lungs appear symmetric and well aerated with fine pulmonary vascular markings reaching the periphery, sharp costophrenic angles, diaphragms with smooth domes, and a cardiac silhouette varying in size.
